    {
      "id": "2094558413519044899",
      "text": "Crazy fast!\n\nThe difference from having 2 DGX Spark instead of one is insane.\n\nI m using with Hermes up to 7 streams with complex coding and agentic tasks and I'm happy when I see over 110 t/s with Qwen 27B and super happy when I look at the stats on my dashboard that tells me that local inference is saving me around $ 17.5K USD a year in cloud API costs. \nI cannot even imagine what that number would  be at the rate you show in the video.\n\nhttps://t.co/sNAxef1YLV",
      "author": {
        "id": "1618273434814881792",
        "name": "AgentSparko 💥",
        "screenName": "AgentSparko",
        "profileImageUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2053381913054683147/6MJgSU7M_normal.jpg",
        "verified": true
      },
      "metrics": {
        "likes": 2,
        "retweets": 0,
        "replies": 0,
        "quotes": 0,
        "views": 540,
        "bookmarks": 3
      },
      "createdAt": "Mon Aug 31 22:50:15 +0000 2026",
      "createdAtLocal": "2026-09-01 06:50",
      "createdAtISO": "2026-08-31T22:50:15+00:00",
      "media": [
        {
          "type": "photo",
          "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HRFdppeWAAAQohz.jpg",
          "width": 1186,
          "height": 825
        }
      ],
      "urls": [],
      "isRetweet": false,
      "retweetedBy": null,
      "lang": "en",
      "score": null,
      "quotedTweet": {
        "id": "2094556895046439201",
        "text": "I made a Hermes skill for task delegation when I use Qwen 27B locally on the DGX Spark and I tell it to create a cron job with a task list to ring each hour and then give it a long task list for coding on multiple projects at the same time. \n\nThe disadvantage is that I do not see anymore on Telegram verbose what it's doing but the advantage is that it speeds things up as it takes advantage of the total throughput of the Spark when concurrency it's high.\n\nIt uses up to 6-7 agents at once...I could push that further as the context pool is not filled even 40% somehow even thou it's around 800K tokens total. \n\nThe best way to check that total throughput it's actually better is to look at my dashboard where it calculates the cloud API cost savings projected from the last hour of work. \n\nWith one stream it stays around $ 7-10K API cost save a year and now that it uses 2-7 streams it stays around $ 17.5K and it keeps finishing jobs and that sets me off from pushing that number higher as I don't know for the moment what other jobs to give it. 😂 \n\nLook at the bottom row to see the 1 year projection.\n\nOne of the agents is now building a Web UI to see thinking traces and actions verbose for all the subagents. 😁",
        "author": {
          "screenName": "AgentSparko",
          "name": "AgentSparko 💥"
        }
      }
    },
